clared bibliographic topology; it does not establish textual identity, critical equivalence, or acceptance.","No source text, translation judgment, semantic relation, rights clearance, human review, graph truth, or canon promotion is created.","This second event-record version refreshes Work input digests after explicit responsibility-claim closure; the 58 topology claim objects and predicates are unchanged.","The seven Work records now reference a separate first-publication chronology claim family; the 58 topology claims and their predicates are unchanged.","The Jenseits 1886 Edition now references separate provision-activity claims and refreshed evidence metadata; the 58 topology claim objects and predicates remain unchanged.","The Genealogie 1892 Edition now references separate provision-activity claims and exact page-return evidence; the 58 topology claim objects and predicates remain unchanged.","The 2007 Cultural Revolution Antonovsky Expression now closes over one exact translated_by responsibility claim and explicitly rejects cross-edition equivalence; the 58 topology claim objects and predicates remain unchanged.","The Antonovsky 1911 fourth Edition adds one source-returnable Work-Expression-Edition-Item route while its own revision-history evidence explicitly blocks cross-edition textual equivalence.","Three provisional Antonovsky 1900, 1903, and 1907 Expression identities first added Work-to-Expression topology claims without inventing Editions, Items, source text, or equivalence.","The exact Lithuanian National Library record adds one provisional Antonovsky 1900 Edition, the exact Russian State Library record adds the 1903 second corrected Edition, and the removed-or-replaced RuNEB card now adds the exact 1907 third Edition. Each has one Expression-to-Edition claim; all remote holdings remain outside ToS Item custody, and the topology set now contains 64 claims.","The exact Reader 1899 route adds one separate uncredited Russian Expression, one exact Edition, and one fragmentary three-part PDF Item. It asserts no translator responsibility, complete 236-page return, 1898 or 1900 derivation, textual equivalence, accepted source text, or redistribution permission; the topology set now contains 67 claims.","The exact Nani 1899 route adds one selected-fragment Russian Expression, one parallel German/Russian Edition witness, and one fixity-verified local RSL/RuNEB PDF Item. Its printed translator and printer statements create separate responsibility and provision claims, while German Expression identity, completeness, derivation, equivalence, accepted text, translation quality, redistribution permission, semantics, and canon remain withheld; the topology set now contains 70 claims.","The exact Internet Archive page-image, scandata, and DjVuXML navigation derivative family remains one separate Item and Edition-to-Item claim without collapsing it into the Commons DjVu, accepting provider OCR, asserting whole-container page or textual identity, authorizing redistribution, or opening translation, semantic, human, or canon work."],"receipt_refs":["ToS/source-witnesses/relations/edition-item/edition-item-claims.jsonl","ToS/source-witnesses/relations/expression-edition/expression-edition-claims.jsonl","ToS/source-witnesses/relations/work-expression/work-expression-claims.jsonl"],"rights_basis_ref":null,"event_version":16,"supersedes_event_ref":null}
